On 18 Dec 1996 06:31:13 GMT, jamesb@aone.com.au (James Burton) wrote:

>Has anyone tried
>
>/sbin/dump -9bf 200 - > /tmp/xxx
>
>or more usefully
>
>/sbin/dump -9bf 200 - | ssh ....

Maybe it's just a syntax error. The argument following the f option
will be interpreted as output file. 
So you should try 
	dump -9 -b 200 -f - ....

I _did_ successfully use piping with 4.0 during conversion from ufs to
advfs. 
	vdump 0f - / | (cd /root; vrestore -xf -)

Matthias




