On Thu, 19 Dec 1996 11:00:36 -0700, Arun Tholudur
<tholudur@optimal.colorado.edu> wrote:

>We have two Alphastations, 200 4/100 and 250 4/266 with 96MB and 128MB
>of RAM respectively currently running digital unix 3.2. Is there any
>advantage to us upgrading to 4.0? We are mainly a number crunching group
>with a lot of numerical computation work. Will we gain anything? Even
>otherwise, is it a pain? Any pointers, suggestions will be appreciated. 
>TIA

;-)
With DU V4.0A, you are no longer limited to 65534 users on a system.
You can now have up to 4.3 billion (american billions) users! :-)))
;-)

The main difference is the new GUI. With 4.0 Digital UNix has the CDE
as default environment. So, working on a graphics terminal is more fun
and easier to new users. Also, many of the system administration
programs now have a GUI.

For more informtaion, you should try to get a copy of the release
notes.

Merry Christmas etc.
Matthias



