CAE Project wrote:
> 
> Hello you experts out there,
> 
> I have a problem with the new CDE based system managemenet system in
> Digital Unix, Sysman. After a machine is installed and someone logs in,
> sysman is automatically launched. How do I prevent that?
> 

There is a file called /var/checklist.setup. This file contains a
timestamp for execution of the SysMan checklist. If you simply create
the file by doing a

date > /var/checklist.setup

then the SysMan checklist will not come up.



