Hi Neil,

Try using the "sysconfig -q inet" command to view your network
parameters.  Also "sysconfig -s" will show you all parameter subsystems
- do a "man" on sysconfig for more information.  To configure the above
parameters the best is probably to to put them into /etc/sysconfigtab
and then reboot.  For more info on the format also do a "man" on
sysconfigtab.

Regards
Paulo
