Chaloemphon Lorattanasane wrote:
> 
> I'm using Digital Unix 4.0a on DEC mothermoard Alpha PC164.
> My graphic adapter is S3 Trio64 with 2MB VRAM. The default
> screen resolution of X server is 1024x768 (256 colors).
> Because I have 2MB VRAM, how can I increase the resolution
> of X server to 1280x1024 (256 colors) ? 

In your /usr/dt/config/Xservers file, modify the last line to specify a
screen resolution. For example, change:



   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0

to

   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -screen 1280



