-- Matthias Kring wrote:
> 
> A simple(?) question: What does MACH stand for.
> 
> I know that thw MACH kernel concept was created at the Carnegie
> Mellon  University, but I cannot find any explanation in DEC's
> manuals what the acronym MACH stands for.
> Just want to know it.

From Addison-Wesley's "Programming under Mach" (Boykin, Kirschen,
Langerman, LoVerso), 1993. In the forward, Rick Rashid (one of the
original developers of Mach) explains that they went through several
attempts at names, without anything sticking. At one point, he says, he
jokingly listed some of the choices to a foreign colleague. The
individual misunderstood Rick's pronunciation of "MUCK" (an acronym for
