Brian Field wrote:
> 
> I've got a DEC 3000/800 running OSF1 V2.0 which panics whenever it
> tries to come up in multiuser mode.  The panic is always reported
> to occur at virtual address 0x00050.  The machine runs fine in single
> user mode.
> 
> Someone mentioned that the problem might be with disk errors on the
> swap partition.  Is there anyway to check the consistency of the
> swap partition (and fix errors) short of reformatting the entire disk
> and reloading the OS.  (The disk is an rz26)
> 
> Thanks
> Brian

You could try disabling the swap device, and see if the box will come up
multi user without it.

Do this by removing the /sbin/swapdefault link (or rename it) and remove
the swap entry from /etc/fstab.  It will complain about running in
overcommittment mode, but should work ok.

