As I recall, the Qualcomm popper recognizes the fact that both Ultrix
and Digital Unix have shadow password abilities.  I believe that the
default compile options in the Makefile specify the use of the
alternate password functions (those used to get at the shadow password
file).  If you aren't using the enhanced security on your box, make
sure you remove the reference to the enhanced security option in the
makefile before building it...

