legend@public.sta.net.cn <Qin Qinghua> wrote:


>      (dbx) patch 0x120001350=0x4421e801
>       >[main,0x120001350]   xor    r1, r1, r1 
>
>     (dbx) 0x120001350/10i
>       >[main,0x120001350]   xor    r1, r1, r1  
>         [main,0x120001354]   call_pal    halt

> The problem is that I want to change the instruction 
> 'lda sp, -352(sp)'
> at address 0x120001350 to that instruction ' xor r1, r1, r1' ONLY, 
> but the next intruction at address 0x120001354 is changed to 
> 'call_pal  halt' unexpectedly.
>
> Why ? Is this a bug of Digital UNIX 3.2D ?

We prefer to think of this as feature (or a consequence).  The
problem is that there is no clear way of specifying that what
you want to change is an instruction, which is 32 bits long.  By
using the address format to the patch command, dbx expects you to 
be changing the quadword, or 64bit value at that address.  But you've
only supplied the (needed) 32 bits, so dbx sign extends for
you and it replaces the whole 64 bit area.  I know I've answered
this exact question internally, so you may have already been informed
of this, but there is something you can do.  Print out the 
hex values of both instructions and change the part that you 
want.  So it would look something like:

(dbx) li
> [main:10, 0x120001310]        addq    r31, 0x14, r16
  [main:10, 0x120001314]        ldq     r17, -32664(gp)
  [main:10, 0x120001318]        ldq     r27, -32456(gp)
  [main:10, 0x12000131c]        jsr     r26, (r27), 0x11fffec90
  [main:10, 0x120001320]        ldah    gp, 8192(r26)
  [main:10, 0x120001324]        lda     gp, 28080(gp)
  [main:11, 0x120001328]        ldq     r27, -32520(gp)
  [main:11, 0x12000132c]        jsr     r26, (r27), 0x120007160
  [main:11, 0x120001330]        ldah    gp, 8192(r26)
  [main:11, 0x120001334]        lda     gp, 28064(gp)
(dbx) 0x120001310/10X
0000000120001310:  a63d806843e29410 6b5b765ca77d8138
0000000120001320:  23bd6db027ba2000 6b5b578ca77d80f8
0000000120001330:  23bd6da027ba2000 a03e0028b01e0028
0000000120001340:  261dfffff4200011 a77d811822107f40
0000000120001350:  27ba20006b5b57df 43e0541023bd6d7c
(dbx) patch 0x120001310 = 0xa63d80684421e801
  [main:10, 0x120001310]        xor     r1, r1, r1
(dbx) 0x120001310/10i
  [main:10, 0x120001310]        xor     r1, r1, r1
  [main:10, 0x120001314]        ldq     r17, -32664(gp)
  [main:10, 0x120001318]        ldq     r27, -32456(gp)
  [main:10, 0x12000131c]        jsr     r26, (r27), 0x11fffec90
  [main:10, 0x120001320]        ldah    gp, 8192(r26)
etc...

PeterT



