Yes they were, altho I don't know how wide the distribution was.  Rice
University obtained several (including serial number 30).  The
machines used the 68000.  The OS was completely different: it was not
a BSD 4 derivative as I recall.  It couldn't be since the 68000 was
not capable of supporting page faulted virtual memory.

Upgrading to a Sun 2 was a board swap: the exterior was still that
clunky old tan and black metal with any one of about 6 different
keyboards (back in those days it sure seemed like Sun changed the
keyboard design weekly).  Although I know some people felt like the
plastic Sun 2 cabinets felt "cheap" and flimsy.

