Slow ls -l is usually caused by many files in the directory and/or having
a lot of entries in /etc/passwd that have to be searched thru to find
the account that owns the file.

Since you're seeing this problem with ps, it's probably a large /etc/passwd
file.  You might consider using NIS to speed things up.


