Alan Way wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> Our sister site in Sydney just had their Alpha die with a CPU-Panic
> message on the console.  Thats OK, but it was followed by a message
> 
> "The zombie walks,  the sequel."
> 
> The message is in our kernel too, along with "The zombie walks!".
> Anyone have any idea what this is about?

It appears to be a 'BSDism', at least it is in a module that
originally came from there.   When a child is exiting (via exit()) it
gets made into a zombie, and then eventually just gets suspended
waiting for the parent to deallocate it.  (It parks on a 
'thread_block()'.   If somehow the thread gets unblocked (instead of 
deallocated), you'll get that message.   I have no idea how that
might happen or if this was a problem that there is a patch for,
etc.  

