Nik Pallatroni (nik@codman.com) wrote:
: J. Cornelis wrote:
: > 
: > We have an Alpha 2100 running OSF/1.  There are problems while printing to
: > a HP Laserjet 5M printer.  Does anyone have a working entry in the
: > /etc/printcap-file ?
: > 
: > I'm appreciate any helps.
: > Thanks
: Is the printer on the network or hanging off the box?  I have HP's on my
: network and use a very simple printcap that looks like this:

: 	printername|lp#:\
: 		:lf=/location of log:\
: 		:rm=printername from host file:\
: 		:rp=text:\ (or raw for ps)
: 		:sd=/spooler location:

: I name them differently for straight text or postscript but they print
: to the same ip.

This works, but at our site, doesn't spool(the lpd/jetdirect daemon on the
printer just blocks and flushes jobs while one job is printing). I believe
that it was designed to work with hp/sun, and with the appropriate s/w from
hp, not as a real UNIX lpd.

We have gone back to using cap, and printing through appletalk.
Works perfectly.

