Oleg Orel (orel@dxunk1) wrote:

: There is very evident problem when you debug kernel of any opereting
: system (my case is OSF1 3.2C). There is possibility, and it's happends
: very often, when system doesn't crash but just stops. In this case I
: dont see way to found point in kernel (device-driver) which introduces
: such events. Is somebody have expirience with such things? Maybe where
: is a way to catch such situation and found the bug(s)??

: Please send copy also by e-mail. 

Well, there are lots of things software can do that causes the
hardware to just stop :-)

On most of the Alpha's, there is a halt button.  If you
press this you should get to the 'console' softare.  At
this point some of the more useful things to try are:

P00>> examine -gpr pc

P00>> examine -gpr ra

P00>> crash

The first two print the program counter and the return address 
that the system was at when you pressed the halt button.  Lots
of times (in my experience) this can be useful information.
The crash command writes a crash dump file that can be read
by the dbx debugger.  Sometime the system is so hosed that
it fails to write the crash dump, so the only info you have
is the examine output.

The Digital document set has an entire manual dedicated to
Kernel Debugging. 

Dave





