Subject: Re: pthreads libraries
Date: 1996/12/05
Message-ID: <32A6D92D.6EEA@zko.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 202504773
references: <kj20d6z4gr.fsf@alpha0.bioch.virginia.edu>
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 3.01Gold (X11; I; OSF1 X4.0 alpha)


William R. Pearson wrote:
> 
> I have just upgraded to Digital Unix 4.0a, and wish to use the pthreads
> libraries rather than cc -threads.
> 
> However, I do not see them anywhere, and cc -pthreads says they cannot
> be found.  I assume I did not install them properly.
> 
> What software kit must I install to get pthreads?

Wrong switch. You want "cc -pthread", not "cc -pthreads". The old
switch, for Draft 4 (DCE) threads and CMA threads was plural, but the
new switch, for POSIX threads, is singular.

The library is /usr/shlib/libpthread.so. If you need to do a manual
link with ld for whatever reason use "-lpthread -lmach -lexc", right
before the "-lc" at the end of the line. You should always compile with
-pthread -- but if you don't, use -D_REENTRANT.

There's no optional kit for threads -- it's part of the base system.

However -- there's no static library (libpthread.a) for threads. You
cannot link a threaded program -non_shared. We'll be restoring
libpthread.a in the future, once kernel interface have stabilized.

