Pierre-Etienne Moreau <moreau@huggy.loria.fr> writes:
> f()
> {
>   g();
> }
> 
> g() is written in assembly and f() in C.
> I would like to know, in g(), the frame pointer of f()
> 
> I spent many hours on this problem, and I did not find any solution.
> 
> If you have any idea, please, send me a mail.
---

The Alpha calling convention doesn't support a frame pointer unless
the function uses alloca() or uses nested procedueres, Thus, you don't
have a frame-pointer in C - the SP is used for everything.

However, see "man unwind" for information that will do what you want.
You'll need a copy of the Alpha calling conventions manual. Postscript
copies are available online, hollar if you need one.



-- 
Dirk Grunwald                 Assoc. Prof, Univ. of Colorado at Boulder



