In article <32A2C8F9.40AE@optusvision.com.au>,
	Richard Begg <richard_begg@optusvision.com.au> writes:
> Michael Livingston wrote:
>> 
>> Is it possible for software to control which tape gets loaded using a
>> TZ877 tape stacker?  I have no problem getting a script to load the tapes
>> in sequence (unloading the current tape, and loading the next).  However,
>> I'd like to be able to load the first tape after finishing with the last
>> tape in the stacker.
>> 
>> Our TZ877s are on DEC Alpha systems running Digital UNIX 3.2C (soon to be
>> 3.2G).
> 
> You can treat these as small jukeboxes by using the SCSI CAM layered
> product to provide a media changer device.  Digital will to try to sell
> you a jukebox license for this sort of thing.  It is certainly needed
> for DEC NSR (legato Networker), but I am not sure if you need it to
> drive the loader directly.

You don't need the Jukebnox license
(Jukebox Tier 1, Part No. QL-04UAL-3B
 Jukebox Tier 2, Part No. QL-04VAL-3B or
 Jukebox Tier 3, Part No. QL-04WAL-3B depending on the model)
unless you are using the "Polycenter Networker" Backup package
(see SPD 50-98-09).

But Digital offers a produkt called "Media Robot Utility" for
