Hi,

Has anyone written a command-line interface for maintaining user disc
quotas? vedquota is great if you only want to change one or two users,
or if you want to copy an entire set of defaults from a prototype user,
but is hopeless for making bulk changes to one or two fields. Something
like 
vchquota [-F limit] [-f limit] [-B limit] [-b limit] [-s setname] user..

is needed.

I can't even see how to write such a utility, because the quotactl(2) 
man page says that only UFS file Systems are supported, and there
is no vquotactl(2) man page.

Our operating system is OSF1 V3.2.

Thanks,
Bob
